# Copy to `.env` and restart `npm run dev`.
#
# If VITE_* is set in your shell/CI, it overrides this file. Unset it for local tunnel dev.
# With `npm run dev`, public-host pages (e.g. bookcomet.net tunnel) always use /api-proxy in code.  # pragma: allowlist secret
#
# --- Local dev (npm run dev) — tunnel or localhost ---
# Proxied to FastAPI on 127.0.0.1:8000; use when the UI is served from a public host  # pragma: allowlist secret
# such as http://bookcomet.net (or any non-localhost origin).  # pragma: allowlist secret
VITE_API_URL=/api-proxy
#
# --- UI shell (erp = default ERP grid; legacy = NodeWorkspace restore) ---
VITE_UI_THEME=erp
# VITE_UI_THEME=legacy
# VITE_LEGACY_WORKSPACE=1
#
# --- Optional: talk to API directly (HTTP UI only, e.g. http://localhost:5173) ---
# VITE_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000  # pragma: allowlist secret
#
# --- Production build (`vite build`) ---
# On HTTPS with VITE_API_URL unset, requests go to same-origin `/api/*` (avoids localhost in the user's browser).
# Your host must proxy `/api` to FastAPI, OR set VITE_API_URL:
# VITE_API_URL=https://bookcometapi.keepocr.com
